9 13194139533788 true] [17592186251167 1041 "field-1" 13194139533788 true] [17592186251167 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251168 13194139533788 true] [17592186251167 1110 #uuid "2f6afa44-4807-5dbb-8586-a1a918d4517b" 13194139533788 true] [17592186251168 1034 "2" 13194139533788 true] [17592186251168 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533788 true] [17592186251168 1111 #uuid "46e8ca14-763b-5506-954f-eb3561049fb8" 13194139533788 true] [17592186251169 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251170 13194139533788 true] [17592186251169 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139533788 true] [17592186251169 1041 "field-2" 13194139533788 true] [17592186251169 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251170 13194139533788 true] [17592186251169 1110 #uuid "8a0c96fe-89a3-5834-ac24-3728fbd2f0a1" 13194139533788 true] [17592186251170 1034 "1" 13194139533788 true] [17592186251170 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533788 true] [17592186251170 1111 #uuid "81a5d834-2e20-5b4d-963a-94cc03176bd2" 13194139533788 true] [17592186251171 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251172 13194139533788 true] [17592186251171 1089 "q-340301" 13194139533788 true] [17592186251171 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139533788 true] [17592186251171 1100 "For the piecewise function \n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}3{e}^{\\,\\,sin(x-1)}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x<1 \\\\ p{x}^{3}\\, & \\text{ for }\\,x\\ge 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nit is known that ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)=3.$ What is the value of the constant $p?$\n\n$p=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533788 true] [17592186251171 1113 #uuid "b91dcbc6-c425-5994-85d5-426529628a2b" 13194139533788 true] [17592186251171 1145 "In order for ${lim}_{x\\to 1}f(x)$ to be equal to $3,$ the left and right-sided limits must both exist and be equal to $3.$\n\n- Approaching from the left, we have $x<1,$ so we use the expression $f(x)=3{e}^{\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x-1)}.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {1}^{-}}3{e}^{\\,\\,sin(x-1)} \\\\  & =3{e}^{\\,\\,sin(1-1)} \\\\  & =3{e}^{\\,\\,sin(0)} \\\\  & =3{e}^{0} \\\\  & 